    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 22 at 5:40AM PDT until October 22 at 8:15AM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Far Southeastern Santa Barbara County in southwestern\nCalifornia...\n\n* WHEN...Until 815 AM PDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas. Rock\nslides and mud slides are possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 539 AM PDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSanta Barbara, Montecito, Carpinteria, Summerland, Rincon Point,\nLa Conchita, Goleta, Mission Canyon and Hope Ranch.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
